WEBVTT

01:18.960 --> 01:20.090
Hayato!

01:20.090 --> 01:21.720
You scum!

01:23.200 --> 01:24.990
I've finally found you!

01:25.960 --> 01:27.530
Son-of-a...

01:27.530 --> 01:29.160
Stop it, both of...

01:33.540 --> 01:35.270
Good God! Don't tell me you killed him too!

01:35.270 --> 01:36.880
Of course not!

01:36.880 --> 01:38.580
Let go! We're still talking!

01:38.580 --> 01:39.910
Don't give me that crap!

01:39.910 --> 01:41.970
Stay out of this!

01:43.110 --> 01:45.880
There's no time for this now!

01:46.950 --> 01:49.150
You go on ahead, I still...

01:49.150 --> 01:51.090
Oh, no, you don't!

01:51.090 --> 01:52.720
Let me go!

01:57.030 --> 02:00.990
Eleventh Night


01:57.030 --> 02:00.990
Darkness, Take My Hand

02:02.800 --> 02:04.770
Where do you think you're going?

02:04.770 --> 02:07.210
There's something I have to find out.

02:07.210 --> 02:08.210
Hold it!

02:08.210 --> 02:09.830
Not now, I said!

02:10.280 --> 02:13.110
You killed Nami...

02:13.110 --> 02:15.140
Yes, about that...

02:16.510 --> 02:20.280
Who told you Mr. Mikogami was the culprit?

02:20.620 --> 02:23.290
Chief Haniwa...

02:23.290 --> 02:28.660
Oh? And how much faith
do you have in him?

02:29.860 --> 02:34.370
You know Hayato would never
kill Nami, don't you?!

02:34.370 --> 02:38.390
Yeah, but he...he...

02:39.540 --> 02:44.510
Whose justice are you trying
to serve right now?

02:44.510 --> 02:47.910
Chief Haniwa's? Or your own?

02:53.080 --> 02:56.420
I'm coming too!
You're not in the clear yet!

02:56.420 --> 02:58.060
Have it your way.

02:58.060 --> 02:59.320
What about you?

02:59.320 --> 03:01.060
I've got to go.

03:01.060 --> 03:03.760
There's something I need to do.

03:15.910 --> 03:17.700
Please excuse me.

03:22.610 --> 03:23.850
It's me.

03:23.850 --> 03:29.910
I'm very sorry. He got away.
They were tougher than we thought.

03:31.220 --> 03:34.990
We got one, but we're down three.

03:35.330 --> 03:38.130
Not very cost-effective.

03:38.900 --> 03:41.490
We'll get him.

03:51.480 --> 03:52.580
We've found him.

03:52.580 --> 03:55.480
We'll regroup and attempt
capture once more.

03:56.250 --> 03:59.150
Yes, carefully now.

04:26.850 --> 04:32.610
In another religion, there is a festival tonight
to celebrate the eve of their savior's birth.

04:33.890 --> 04:40.520
But for us, tonight is the night that marks
the beginning of a new era!

04:40.890 --> 04:44.620
Here, in this town!

05:03.820 --> 05:07.150
Oh dear, that was too easy.

05:08.250 --> 05:10.220
You don't have very good guards.

05:11.420 --> 05:14.880
I'm not really worth guarding anymore.

05:15.430 --> 05:17.050
Who are you?

05:17.600 --> 05:21.660
Let's just say I'm an Ally of Justice.

05:31.480 --> 05:33.540
It's snowing.

05:34.580 --> 05:37.220
I hate snow.

05:37.220 --> 05:44.020
It hides everything: The beauty of a flower,
and the ugliness of Man.

05:48.490 --> 05:50.980
Wait, Hayato! What's going on?

05:51.360 --> 05:53.730
What is it you have to find out?

05:53.730 --> 05:55.370
Why a church?!

05:55.370 --> 05:56.990
Hey!

06:08.080 --> 06:09.710
It's her!

06:14.720 --> 06:16.980
Who's that woman?

06:17.320 --> 06:19.020
Ha-Hayato?!

06:19.590 --> 06:21.290
Right this way.

06:25.400 --> 06:27.500
You two will have to wait.

06:27.500 --> 06:30.470
Like hell I will! And let my suspect waltz off?!

06:30.470 --> 06:31.440
Sorry.
Like hell I will! And let my suspect waltz off?!

06:32.870 --> 06:35.500
I've got to go in alone.

06:35.670 --> 06:37.700
Oh, isn't that perfect?!

06:38.380 --> 06:41.240
Please, trust in Hayato.

06:43.080 --> 06:45.210
I appreciate this.

06:45.580 --> 06:47.210
Thank you.

06:48.220 --> 06:50.020
Don't try running off, now!

06:51.320 --> 06:52.890
Still...

06:52.890 --> 06:55.720
Why rig such an elaborate device?

07:17.750 --> 07:19.620
You?!

07:19.620 --> 07:21.780
Was it really you?!

07:25.420 --> 07:27.690
Why did you kill Nami?

07:29.090 --> 07:35.330
To destroy evil, you have to
become a greater evil.

07:38.040 --> 07:42.700
Perhaps it's time you
removed your mask too?

07:43.710 --> 07:48.710
The time has long come and gone.

07:48.710 --> 07:51.010
Do you still want to know?

07:51.680 --> 07:54.380
Yes, all of it.

07:58.120 --> 07:59.850
Come, then.

08:04.060 --> 08:06.730
I didn't want to believe it.

08:06.730 --> 08:10.060
Did Tetsuro tell you?

08:12.870 --> 08:14.740
Why...

08:15.140 --> 08:18.270
Why have you done this, Yoshio?

08:19.110 --> 08:23.670
GRO should never have fallen
into human hands.

08:24.850 --> 08:28.110
That's true of this mask too.

08:28.450 --> 08:31.180
It must not exist in our world.

08:31.720 --> 08:34.560
That's why you killed Nami?!

08:34.560 --> 08:37.390
And Sayo, no less?

08:41.670 --> 08:44.360
I don't get it. I don't get it!

08:44.840 --> 08:49.360
The Yoshio Kanzaki I know
could never kill anyone!

08:49.610 --> 08:53.340
The Yoshio Kanzaki you knew...

08:53.750 --> 08:55.370
...is dead.

08:56.180 --> 09:00.140
He died in the jungle, in Southeast Asia.

09:01.990 --> 09:03.720
The enemy's attacking!

09:03.720 --> 09:05.810
Get down, quick! They'll get you!

09:35.190 --> 09:38.380
That was when I met them.

09:40.090 --> 09:45.360
They were defying fate and
attempting to escape.

09:45.360 --> 09:48.420
I wanted to protect them.

09:49.300 --> 09:54.260
In the end, they wound up protecting me.

09:54.670 --> 09:56.300
Yoshio?!

09:59.210 --> 10:04.480
When I think back, perhaps it was
all the Hand of Destiny.

10:05.320 --> 10:05.870
Mr. Yoshi
Kanzaki

10:06.920 --> 10:08.250
Mr. Yoshi
Kanzaki

10:08.250 --> 10:09.390
Mr. Yoshi
Kanzaki

10:08.250 --> 10:09.390
Yoshio,

10:09.390 --> 10:10.010
Yoshio,

10:10.120 --> 10:14.990
By the time you read this,
I will no longer be in this world.

10:16.290 --> 10:23.560
Before I entrust myself entirely to God,
I wanted to write you a letter.

10:42.620 --> 10:47.180
In the end, the relics from
Kagura Village were excavated?

10:48.430 --> 10:50.050
Yes...

10:54.230 --> 11:00.670
When you saw this, you pressed
Tatsuyuki Kagura to research it?

11:00.670 --> 11:02.540
No, I didn't.

11:03.140 --> 11:06.780
Kagura went forward with the research himself,
becoming completely immersed.

11:06.780 --> 11:09.310
It was like he was possessed.

11:09.310 --> 11:12.910
I suppose he didn't think
there was any danger?

11:13.750 --> 11:18.590
Even a child can tell you that
something that's still alive

11:18.590 --> 11:23.890
after being buried for thousands, no,
tens of thousands of years is dangerous!

11:25.260 --> 11:27.370
Good point.

11:27.370 --> 11:31.200
Still, you provided the funding, right?

11:31.200 --> 11:34.440
Well, the more dangerous something is,
the more it's worth.

11:34.440 --> 11:38.430
But Kagura became possessed of
some strange ideals.

11:38.910 --> 11:41.850
When a grown man starts
touting lofty dreams,

11:41.850 --> 11:47.080
he can either go into politics
or religion, right?

11:47.080 --> 11:51.150
So, that was the basis for
the White Bell Society?

11:53.020 --> 11:55.530
He was a guileless man.

11:55.530 --> 12:01.830
So guileless that eventually he stopped being
a researcher and became a religious leader.

12:02.100 --> 12:08.540
Religion is profitable, but the truly
faithful aren't interested in profit.

12:08.540 --> 12:11.310
He was just a stubborn mule.

12:11.310 --> 12:15.540
So, you used force to try to get hold of it.

12:16.750 --> 12:18.480
That's right.

12:26.920 --> 12:29.630
Assigning Haniwa to the task was a mistake.

12:29.630 --> 12:30.360
Kagura
Pharmaceuticals
New
Project
Plan

12:29.630 --> 12:30.360

Assigning Haniwa to the task was a mistake.

12:30.360 --> 12:32.360
Kagura
Pharmaceuticals
New
Project
Plan


12:30.360 --> 12:32.360
That idiot always goes overboard.

12:32.360 --> 12:33.130
That idiot always goes overboard.

12:33.130 --> 12:33.400
Gago
Project


12:33.130 --> 12:33.400
That idiot always goes overboard.

12:33.400 --> 12:34.830
Gago
Project


12:49.780 --> 12:54.680
After the fire, we found two bodies that we
assumed were Kagura and his son.

12:55.390 --> 12:59.120
The prize, too, was destroyed in the fire.

12:59.120 --> 13:01.530
Or so you thought.

13:01.530 --> 13:10.430
Yes, we never found out who was
moving in the shadows.

13:10.430 --> 13:17.500
And somehow or other, it found its way to
Tatsuo Kagura and the Phantom was born.

13:18.080 --> 13:22.840
But is the Phantom really Tatsuo Kagura?

13:24.480 --> 13:26.680
You tell me!

13:29.920 --> 13:33.980
There is one thing of which I am sure.

13:34.090 --> 13:37.360
This was not to be possessed by humankind.

13:37.830 --> 13:41.590
But I could not destroy it,

13:41.700 --> 13:45.860
nor could I abandon it to a dark abyss
where it would never again be found.

13:45.970 --> 13:49.960
When the time comes, it will be
your decision what to do.

13:50.070 --> 13:55.480
Forgive me for leaving its
dark powers in your hands.

13:55.780 --> 13:59.150
The first time I put it on,

13:59.150 --> 14:02.950
I nearly drowned in its power.

14:03.420 --> 14:09.190
It was stronger, more overwhelming
than any prayer to God.

14:09.790 --> 14:16.300
My brother and I knew instinctively
that it had given birth to us,

14:16.300 --> 14:19.700
and we knew what we had to do.

14:19.940 --> 14:23.610
I knew too.

14:23.610 --> 14:27.100
The duty of the one who wears the Mask...

14:29.610 --> 14:31.550
Stop! Don't move!

14:31.820 --> 14:35.820
There's something I have to do.

14:35.820 --> 14:38.450
Maya...Miss Maya is...

14:38.790 --> 14:41.490
Maya Kuroshio?! What about her?!

14:41.490 --> 14:45.930
She's going to become the Cocoon of Chaos!

14:45.930 --> 14:47.730
The Cocoon of Chaos?

14:48.000 --> 14:54.700
Yes, all of the terrible karma that has been
sealed away will be released!

14:54.910 --> 14:57.670
Her body will serve as the womb.

14:57.840 --> 15:00.170
A new human species is to be born!

15:07.250 --> 15:08.920
Don't!

15:08.920 --> 15:10.680
How can you kill the woman you love?!

15:13.360 --> 15:18.160
It's me, remember? I understand
a thing or two about you!

15:18.660 --> 15:22.030
If you understand, let me go.

15:22.400 --> 15:25.670
You're hurt! What can you do?
I mean, this thing...

15:25.670 --> 15:27.510
Don't touch it!

15:27.510 --> 15:29.530
I won't let you have it!

15:30.240 --> 15:31.870
Yoshio...

15:32.540 --> 15:34.270
Not you.

15:34.980 --> 15:40.710
Not you, of all people! Don't ever touch it!

15:42.350 --> 15:46.650
Miss Maya is Maya Kagura, and...

15:51.330 --> 15:52.860
Now, come out!

15:52.860 --> 15:55.960
Or do I have to burn you out?

16:00.200 --> 16:02.230
What the...

16:02.540 --> 16:04.470
Hey! Are you okay?!

16:06.110 --> 16:07.480
What happened?

16:07.480 --> 16:10.010
I don't know, but...

16:10.010 --> 16:12.220
I heard two explosions.

16:12.220 --> 16:15.450
That bastard better not have croaked!

16:15.850 --> 16:20.190
Of course not! Of course Hayato's not...

16:21.560 --> 16:23.250
You...

16:25.160 --> 16:28.500
What should we do?
The Children's Center is in danger!

16:28.500 --> 16:31.600
We've got to save the kids first! Let's go!

16:31.600 --> 16:33.230
Right...

16:37.980 --> 16:40.540
We smoked out a pair of rats!

16:40.540 --> 16:42.210
Leave them to me.

16:42.210 --> 16:45.710
Remember your job now.
Take it nice and easy.

16:48.990 --> 16:52.010
I'll take the pussy cat.

16:52.360 --> 16:54.880
It's a fire! The church is burning!

16:55.690 --> 16:57.030
Father Kanzaki!

16:57.030 --> 16:58.860
It's okay, it's okay...

16:58.860 --> 17:00.230
Is everyone all right?

17:00.230 --> 17:00.660
Kiriko!

17:00.660 --> 17:01.900
Stay right there!
Kiriko!

17:01.900 --> 17:02.470
Stay right there!

17:02.470 --> 17:04.870
It's dangerous outside! Don't come out!

17:07.200 --> 17:11.710
You go around back and get the kids.
I'll get the bus!

17:11.710 --> 17:13.340
Got it.

17:15.550 --> 17:17.280
You monster...

17:17.280 --> 17:18.940
You're in the way, rat!

17:21.120 --> 17:25.090
You want to know what I did for
fun on the battlefield?

17:25.090 --> 17:29.120
Burning people alive while they
begged for their lives!

17:29.430 --> 17:31.390
How...How could you?!

17:32.260 --> 17:35.490
This is fun! Watch!

17:36.400 --> 17:39.230
Stop! Don't hurt the children!

17:40.540 --> 17:43.230
Oh, that face! I love it!

17:46.840 --> 17:49.110
Stop it, you monster!

17:49.680 --> 17:54.740
Pipe down, girly! You're ruining my fun!

17:56.790 --> 17:59.690
Oh, yes! That's the face!

18:05.060 --> 18:07.190
Time to go beddy-bye.

18:11.940 --> 18:13.770
Finally, the man of the hour...

18:14.210 --> 18:15.140
Wait...

18:15.140 --> 18:16.330
Move!
Wait...

18:21.010 --> 18:25.640
Ha! So, much for the wounded beast.

18:35.230 --> 18:37.420
Still not dead?

18:44.700 --> 18:47.190
Fool, rushing in during a battle!

19:15.630 --> 19:18.400
The night's still young.

19:25.410 --> 19:27.570
Now, let's have a song.

19:28.810 --> 19:31.610
We've got a long night ahead of us.

19:42.330 --> 19:43.990
It's over now!

19:50.700 --> 19:52.760
You...

19:55.670 --> 19:59.230
Don't underestimate me.

20:02.380 --> 20:06.370
The wildfire by Kagura Dam is still burning!
No word yet on casualties!

20:06.820 --> 20:09.750
Roger. I've contacted the local fire precinct.
They're on the way.

20:09.750 --> 20:12.810
The weather's bad. Hurry, please.

20:21.670 --> 20:23.290
Shit...

20:26.770 --> 20:28.430
Move in!

20:57.000 --> 20:59.970
It's going to be a long night.

21:03.210 --> 21:12.310
There is only one sky,
though the world is large

21:12.450 --> 21:16.990
When you lose sight of the one you love

21:16.990 --> 21:22.580
Look up at it for strength

21:22.730 --> 21:31.870
The path we walked together
now splits into two

21:31.870 --> 21:40.710
Our tears show how much
we long to meet again

21:40.980 --> 21:45.550
The you of tomorrow will be born tomorrow

21:45.550 --> 21:50.720
Just as the Sun rises after a long night

21:50.720 --> 21:54.730
Throw away all the rest of the dream

21:54.730 --> 21:58.990
And open your arms!

21:59.230 --> 22:03.870
The future is always right before your eyes

22:03.870 --> 22:08.870
Just waiting for you to step forward

22:08.870 --> 22:12.980
Beyond the horizon

22:12.980 --> 22:20.780
A world awaits you, and new encounters

22:24.520 --> 22:24.590
A holy night...

22:24.590 --> 22:26.260
Twelfth Night


22:24.590 --> 22:26.260
Bloody Eve

22:24.590 --> 22:26.260

A holy night...

22:26.260 --> 22:33.360
Twelfth Night


22:26.260 --> 22:33.360
Bloody Eve

22:26.260 --> 22:33.360

Red blankets whiteness, and the flames of
Purgatory engulf the City of Sin.

22:33.360 --> 22:36.500
Twelfth Night


22:33.360 --> 22:36.500
Bloody Eve

22:33.360 --> 22:36.500

For whom does the bell toll?

22:36.500 --> 22:37.190
Twelfth Night


